      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Part 4 - Process ID (PID)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Part 4 - Process ID (PID)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-dyFAv70XHmmQI_Q78oU7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2000.9233171076967,
      "y": 15810.90231034308,
      "width": 594,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1502758781,
      "version": 54,
      "versionNonce": 1064913331,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785423436143,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every process has a unique identifier.\nPID = 5012\nLinux uses the PID to manage:\n\nScheduling\nSignals\nMemory\nCPU allocation\nProcess termination\n\nYou can view running processes with:\nps or ps -ef\n\nExample output:\n\nUID     PID   PPID  CMD\namit   4021  3980  python app.py\namit   4100  3980  nginx\nNotice the PID column.\n\n\nWhy Do We Need a PID?\nImagine 500 Python programs are running.\nIf you want to stop one of them:\n    kill 4021\n\nHow does Linux know which one?\nBecause every process has its own PID.\nWithout a PID, process management would be impossible.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every process has a unique identifier.\nPID = 5012\nLinux uses the PID to manage:\n\nScheduling\nSignals\nMemory\nCPU allocation\nProcess termination\n\nYou can view running processes with:\nps or ps -ef\n\nExample output:\n\nUID     PID   PPID  CMD\namit   4021  3980  python app.py\namit   4100  3980  nginx\nNotice the PID column.\n\n\nWhy Do We Need a PID?\nImagine 500 Python programs are running.\nIf you want to stop one of them:\n    kill 4021\n\nHow does Linux know which one?\nBecause every process has its own PID.\nWithout a PID, process management would be impossible.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "QCHvyxfVoAC7E1_M-f1QK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1919.2319108576967,
      "y": 16628.17184159308,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
