      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Should a Backend Engineer Care?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Should a Backend Engineer Care?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4NgVf_0f38AFO1NcRMhoQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2060.3647233576967,
      "y": 21924.91012284308,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIo",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1785083187,
      "version": 88,
      "versionNonce": 2073483709,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785424978449,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Imagine your Django application is deployed using Gunicorn.\nYou don't start it manually every time.\nInstead, you create a systemd service\n\nSystemd -> gunicorm -> django\nIf Gunicorn crashes,\nsystemd can restart it automatically.\nThis is how many production servers are configure\n\nCheck It Yourself\nSee PID 1: ps -p 1\n\nOn most Linux distributions, you'll see:\nPID TTY          TIME CMD\n1 ?        00:00:02 systemd\n\nNow list running services:\n    systemctl list-units --type=service\n\nCheck one service:systemctl status ssh or systemctl status docker\n\n(depending on what's installed).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Imagine your Django application is deployed using Gunicorn.\nYou don't start it manually every time.\nInstead, you create a systemd service\n\nSystemd -> gunicorm -> django\nIf Gunicorn crashes,\nsystemd can restart it automatically.\nThis is how many production servers are configure\n\nCheck It Yourself\nSee PID 1: ps -p 1\n\nOn most Linux distributions, you'll see:\nPID TTY          TIME CMD\n1 ?        00:00:02 systemd\n\nNow list running services:\n    systemctl list-units --type=service\n\nCheck one service:systemctl status ssh or systemctl status docker\n\n(depending on what's installed).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
